`docs/design.md` is now written for Taiga #5, confirming this stage is a no-op: the feature is entirely backend-internal (write-on-mutation, load-on-construct), no route shapes, no frontend files, and no new user-visible state are introduced, so there's nothing for the ux-designer role to specify. It traces each acceptance criterion to why no design element applies and hands off directly to the developer stage.